Hi! I'm Mia, a grad student working on a distributed systems project with my labmate Theo. We're building a distributed cache and want to call the repository distributed-cache-lab. Since we're collaborating, I'd like a main branch for stable code and separate dev branches for each of us: dev-mia and dev-theo. Could you initialize the README.md file on main with: "# Distributed Cache Lab

A research project exploring distributed caching strategies and eviction policies for high-throughput systems."? I'd also like a basic lru_cache.py file on main with: "# In-memory LRU cache skeleton
class LRUCache:
    def __init__(self, capacity):
        self.capacity = capacity
        self.store = {}

    def get(self, key):
        return self.store.get(key)"

I've been reading up on caching internals, so could you copy lru_policy.go from dgraph-io's ristretto repository onto my branch? Theo has been studying LFU eviction, so could you also copy arc_policy.go from hashicorp's golang-lru repository onto his branch? Finally, please create a pull request from dev-mia to main with the title "Add LRU cache skeleton" and description "This PR adds the initial LRU cache skeleton for the distributed caching lab."
